Q: How to direct calculate the range of a float in C? A: <p>I think it would be a lot easier if you would use the sizeof() operator.<br />
You prevent looping around, and you avoid hardcoding sizes.<br />
For example:</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#include &lt;math.h&gt;

unsigned short unsigned_short_max()
{
    int n = sizeof(unsigned short) * 8;//for byte to bit conversion 
    return (pow(2, n) - 1);
}

int main()
{
    printf(&quot;The range of an unsigned short is from 0 to %u\n&quot;, unsigned_short_max());
    return 0;
}
</code></pre>

